From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 05:18:19 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Video layer: what covers the video is noted; an edge band is
 cut out

Build 134 never raised the video panel: something of the page was in front
of the video in every composite. WR now passes the box the page covers in
front of the video and how many tiles do it; the layer notes it, and when
all of it lies in a band along the top or bottom edge (at most a twelfth of
the visible height -- a player's progress bar) the panel still goes above
the browser with that band cut out of it, so the band shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp                   | 126 +++++++++++++++---
 gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs          |  44 ++++--
 2 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gfx/webrender_bindings/GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp b/gfx/webrender_bindings/GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp
index 9c16dbe575..22238eb8aa 100644
--- a/gfx/webrender_bindings/GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp
+++ b/gfx/webrender_bindings/GeckoW10mVideoLayer.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 #include <dxgi1_3.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <atomic>
 #include <math.h>
 
@@ -54,7 +55,10 @@ struct GeckoW10mVideoLayerSink {
   // a hardware overlay only above (the test in build 132: under the
   // browser it was composed by the GPU whatever else was done), and above
   // it hides whatever the page draws over the video.
-  void (*stack)(int32_t aAbove);
+  // aTrimTop/aTrimBottom: rows of the visible part, in the browser surface's
